        <strong>Abstract</strong>—In modern embedded systems pedagogy, the convergence of physical edge nodes and real-time laboratory tracking poses severe concurrency and cryptographic overheads. This article presents the complete architecture of <em>VoltCore Apex Academia</em>, a modular learning platform integrating an ESP32 hardware telemetry node with an OWASP-compliant SQLite database utilizing PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (260,000 iterations). By offloading SPI frame decoding for 13.56MHz MFRC522 RFID tokens to FreeRTOS Core 1 and servicing HTTP/REST JSON payloads over Core 0, deterministic sub-15ms verification latency is maintained. A zero-latency Wokwi simulation sandbox and a Gemini AI-driven viva voce mentor are integrated, enabling students to simulate circuit topologies, debug clock stretching, and validate laboratory competencies against Anna University R2021 curriculum benchmarks.
        <div class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#00F0B5]">
